# Thallium · Tl · gate 81

**Thallium** (Tl) is element **81** of the periodic table — a **post-transition metal**, period 6, group 13, p-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **204.38**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
'The poisoner's poison' — tasteless, deadly; once the rat-killer and the spy's tool.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **81** falls on **0:1 — first valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **0**. That state is *the first reach of emptiness toward one — potential, charge, the rising edge* — the nature of emergence here is **electrical**. Thallium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — electrical
This emergent carries the **electrical** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#3fd0e0`.

